      </div>
      <div>
        <details class="seo-faq">
          <summary>Is SMETA certification available?</summary>
          <div class="ans">No. &#8220;SMETA certification&#8221; is a common search term, but SMETA is an audit methodology. Its output is an audit report, not a certificate.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-faq">
          <summary>Is Sedex membership the same as certification?</summary>
          <div class="ans">No. Membership provides access to Sedex services and the platform. It does not certify a company&#8217;s compliance.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-faq">
          <summary>Who can conduct a SMETA audit?</summary>
          <div class="ans">SMETA audits must be conducted through a Sedex-approved Affiliate Audit Company and its authorized auditors. EUROCERT SA appears in Sedex&#8217;s official AAC list.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-faq">
          <summary>Do I need a 2-Pillar or 4-Pillar audit?</summary>
          <div class="ans">Follow your buyer&#8217;s requirements. A 4-Pillar audit includes extended environmental assessment and business ethics in addition to the two core pillars.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-faq">
          <summary>How long is a SMETA report valid?</summary>
          <div class="ans">SMETA is not a certificate with a standard expiry date. Confirm the required audit frequency with your buyer, taking account of site risks and follow-up requirements.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-faq">
          <summary>Can I share the report with several buyers?</summary>
          <div class="ans">Reports can be shared through the Sedex Platform, subject to access arrangements and each buyer&#8217;s requirements.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-faq">
          <summary>Does one audit automatically cover multiple factories?</summary>
          <div class="ans">No. Provide details of all sites and workplaces so the audit team can confirm the correct scope and reporting arrangements.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
